@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy | Yintong Zhou</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for the ZYT personal website, including information about technical logs, voluntary email contacts and GDPR rights." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="/privacy" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
</HeadContent>

<article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
        This privacy policy explains how this personal website (the “Website”) handles personal data in accordance with
        Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (the “GDPR”). The Website is a personal portfolio and does not provide user accounts,
        user registration, contact forms, comments or personalised services.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
    <p>
        The data controller is Yintong Zhou. For privacy-related requests, you can contact the controller at
        <a href="mailto:contactdm.yt@gmail.com">contactdm.yt@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Personal data collected</h2>
    <p>
        The Website does not intentionally collect personal data through forms, accounts, registrations or marketing
        tools. You can browse the publicly available pages without providing your name, email address or other personal
        information.
    </p>
    <p>
        As with any website, the hosting infrastructure may temporarily process technical information needed to deliver
        and secure the Website, such as IP address, request date and time, requested resource, browser information and
        error or security events. This information is handled by the hosting provider in its role as infrastructure
        provider and is not used by the controller to create user profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Voluntary communications</h2>
    <p>
        If you voluntarily contact the controller by email, the controller will process the information contained in your
        message, including your email address and any information you choose to provide, only to respond to your request
        and manage the correspondence.
    </p>
    <p>
        The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where the request concerns steps prior to a contract, or Article 6(1)(f)
        GDPR based on the legitimate interest in replying to communications and protecting the controller’s rights.
        Messages are kept only for as long as reasonably necessary to handle the request and any related legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
        The Website does not intentionally use analytics, advertising, profiling or social tracking cookies. It does not
        store preferences or identifiers in the browser. Strictly necessary technical storage may be used by the hosting
        infrastructure or security components where required to operate the Website; this is not used for marketing or
        behavioural tracking.
    </p>
    <p>
        For more information, see the <NavLink href="Cookie">Cookie Policy</NavLink>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Recipients and external links</h2>
    <p>
        Data may be accessible to hosting, security and email service providers only when necessary for the purposes above.
        The Website also contains links to third-party websites, such as GitHub and LinkedIn. Those services operate as
        independent controllers under their own privacy policies when you visit them. The controller is not responsible for
        their processing activities.
    </p>

    <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
        The controller does not intentionally transfer personal data outside the European Economic Area. A provider used
        for hosting or email may process data in another country; where this occurs, the provider is responsible for using
        an appropriate GDPR transfer mechanism, such as an adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>
        Subject to the conditions and limitations established by the GDPR, you may request access to, rectification or
        erasure of your personal data, restriction of processing, data portability, or object to processing based on
        legitimate interests. Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw consent at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
        To exercise your rights, contact <a href="mailto:contactdm.yt@gmail.com">contactdm.yt@gmail.com</a>. You also have
        the right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority, in Italy the
        <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may be updated when the Website or its processing activities change. The latest version will always be
        published on this page.
    </p>
</article>